# Git Worktree Workflow

Feature work happens in **git worktrees** under `worktrees/` (gitignored). Do not confuse
this directory with **`git stash`** — that command shelves uncommitted changes temporarily.

## HARD GATE

Before editing tracked files: `pwd` must be under `worktrees/` and branch must not be `main`.
If either check fails, create a worktree first.

## Create a worktree

```bash
git worktree add worktrees/<name> -b feature/<name>
cd worktrees/<name>
```

## Merge and cleanup (local)

From the main working tree:

```bash
git checkout main
git merge feature/<branch-name>
git worktree remove --force worktrees/<name>
git branch -d feature/<branch-name>
git worktree prune
ls worktrees/    # verify no zombie directories remain
```

Notes:

- `cd` to the main working tree **before** `git worktree remove` — removing while cwd is inside the worktree leaves a partial directory.
- `--force` on remove when needed after merge (worktree contents differ from branch tip).
- Run project pre-merge checks from the worktree before merging (lint, tests, pre-commit — see project rules).

## List worktrees

```bash
git worktree list
```

## Move a worktree

```bash
git worktree move worktrees/<old-name> worktrees/<new-name>
```
